---
import GuideLayout from '../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<GuideLayout title="Introduction" description="Community build guide for 33 Immortals — weapon upgrades, perks, relics, and build strategies.">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">Community build guide for 33 Immortals — weapon upgrades, perks, relics, and build strategies.</p>

  <section>
    <p>This is a community-built guide for <strong>33 Immortals</strong>, covering weapon upgrades, perks, relics, and build strategy. The site mirrors the <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A-ihBD9WTGZl7Yi2OqbQJL6gN_2sA2AX3gWuCNvlQ90/edit?tab=t.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">original Google Doc</a> in a web-friendly format with sidebar navigation and a light/dark theme.</p>

    <Callout>
      <strong>Last updated:</strong> February 10, 2026 — Update 6 (Gluttony Update).<br />
      <strong>Note:</strong> Hooks coverage stays partly WIP until bugs are fixed (or not).
    </Callout>

    <h2 id="what-this-guide-is">What this guide is</h2>
    <p>This guide won't teach you much about how to <em>play</em> 33 Immortals — there are some weapon tips along the way — but it does give a deeper understanding of meta-building and weapon differences.</p>
    <p>The build list does not try to cover every possible build, either because the author doesn't know about a specific one, or because another build does the same job better. <strong>It's not about ranking builds, but sharing some interesting ones.</strong> If you find a build you like that isn't here, keep playing it (and please share it). We need build diversity.</p>
    <p>Build "core DPS" figures shown later are estimates at 0 atk, no costrike, no crit, 100% uptime, every attack hitting (unrealistic on some builds), every condition optimal, and on a single target. Take them with a pinch of salt — cleave, range, costrike-per-sec for crit buildup, and many other factors matter too.</p>

    <h2 id="how-to-read">How to read the site</h2>
    <p>Use the left sidebar to navigate. The recommended order on a first pass:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><a href={`${base}general-tips`}>General Tips</a> — core habits.</li>
      <li><a href={`${base}damage`}>Damage</a> — formulas behind every hit.</li>
      <li><a href={`${base}empathy-coop`}>Empathy & Coop Powers</a> — how teamwork scales.</li>
      <li><a href={`${base}ordeals`}>Ordeals & Agony</a> — difficulty modifiers and effective damage reduction.</li>
      <li><a href={`${base}perks`}>Perks</a> and <a href={`${base}relics`}>Relics</a> — what's available to slot.</li>
      <li><a href={`${base}making-a-build`}>Making a Build</a> — how it all comes together.</li>
      <li>Finally, dig into specific <strong>weapon pages</strong> for upgrades, tips, and curated builds.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
    <p>Thanks to <strong>Romalllka</strong>, <strong>.tobbez</strong>, <strong>sejemsom</strong>, <strong>Kitty_sparkles</strong>, and <strong>Wasted_Warlord (N00b)</strong> for help on various points. Thanks to <strong>Jack</strong> for the 3D weapon models referenced in the source doc.</p>
    <p>Portuguese version by <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_xQwSP1V-NoP4kxBuQGTGn5h7Of_BgrUcGwxK37k4po/edit?tab=t.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@Kakerucchi</a>.</p>
    <p>Contact for suggestions: <code>__to</code> on Discord (<code>@to</code> on TLG).</p>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
